  "reading_list": [],
  "quiz_markdown": "### Q1. Turnaround often uses I–vi–ii–V in jazz.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q2. Phrygian half uses ♭II–V in minor.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q3. Advanced cadences appear in classical analysis.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q4. Evaded cadence surprises the listener.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q5. Not every historical cadence appears in folk session music.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q6. Turnaround repeats each chorus.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q7. Baroque music uses cadential formulas extensively.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q8. Representative depth means patterns not exhaustive catalogs.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q9. Cadence study supports form analysis.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q10. Jazz ii–V–I is applied cadence chain.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q11. Phrygian half is named for lowered second scale degree.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q12. Advanced tier completes cadence spiral.\n\n**Answer:** True",
